{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nAccepted `/rerun` and `recheck-review` requests are currently represented only by a forced event in the process-local asyncio queue. If the receiver exits before that event is processed, the request disappears. Local dedup and the existing Gerrit `LLM-Review` vote then cause reconciliation to skip the revision.\n\nThe approved contract uses Gerrit as the durable source of truth: an accepted request first changes the exact revision to no nonzero `LLM-Review` vote. That label write also emits a fresh Gerrit `comment-added` event carrying the revision and ref, re-admitting even an old change to the reconciler’s events-log window. No `forced_pending` table is introduced.\n\n## Proven root cause and capability evidence\n\nBoth acceptance paths currently reset the attempt budget and enqueue/return a forced event without first creating durable state. Reconciliation checks local `voted` state before Gerrit and therefore skips a revision whose stale local row survives after its Gerrit vote is reset. `review_and_vote` has the same local-first guard.\n\nA read-only probe of the production Gerrit events-log on 2026-08-09 found 551 `LLM-Review` approval events. Every one was a `comment-added` event with both `patchSet.revision` and `patchSet.ref`; observed values included `0`, `-1`, and `1`. This verifies the load-bearing capability: a review-label write produces the fresh patchset-bearing event the reconciler consumes, independently of the original patchset-created event’s age.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Add a Gerrit operation that writes `LLM-Review: 0` plus a rerun-request message on the exact revision, thereby durably changing vote state and emitting a fresh patchset-bearing event.\n2. After the reset POST succeeds, read the exact revision’s votes and require that no account has a nonzero `LLM-Review` vote. If a concurrent/admin vote remains or the verification read fails, reject the request without resetting attempts, enqueueing work, or posting an affirmative acknowledgement.\n3. For accepted `/rerun` and `recheck-review`, reset the Gerrit vote first, verify the no-nonzero-vote postcondition, reset the retry-attempt budget, then enqueue/return the forced event.\n4. Reconcile only the bounded candidate set in the existing events-log window. For each candidate, query Gerrit before trusting local dedup. A successful no-nonzero-vote result deletes only that revision’s stale local `voted` row and invokes the ordinary voter. The existing Gerrit-error branch remains fail-closed, preserves dedup, and holds the cursor back for retry.\n5. Preserve the normal skip when Gerrit has any nonzero vote. Preserve the forced live path for the accepted request already in memory.\n6. Prove the complete restart path with a stateful Gerrit fake: the reset operation appends a production-shaped `comment-added` event after an already-advanced cursor; a new process queue starts empty; reconciliation consumes the fresh event, clears stale dedup, and reviews the exact revision.\n7. Run focused review-bot tests and repository gates.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Unit/API test: `/rerun` resets the exact revision’s Gerrit `LLM-Review` vote before resetting attempts.\n- [ ] Unit/API test: `/rerun` returns HTTP 202 only after a successful reset and a successful read proving no nonzero vote remains.\n- [ ] Unit/API failure test: reset failure, verification-read failure, or a remaining nonzero vote returns non-success, leaves attempts unchanged, and enqueues nothing.\n- [ ] Unit/retrigger test: accepted `recheck-review` resets and verifies the exact revision before resetting attempts or producing a forced event.\n- [ ] Unit/retrigger failure test: reset failure, verification-read failure, or a remaining nonzero vote produces no forced event and posts no affirmative accepted reply.\n- [ ] Stateful reconciliation test: the reset appends a production-shaped patchset-bearing `comment-added` event newer than an already-advanced cursor.\n- [ ] Stateful restart test: with an empty replacement queue and retained stale local dedup, reconciliation consumes that fresh event and reviews the exact revision.\n- [ ] Stateful invariant test: recovery deletes only the matching stale `voted` row and preserves unrelated rows.\n- [ ] Contrast test: reconciliation skips a revision when Gerrit carries any nonzero `LLM-Review` vote.\n- [ ] Error-path test: a Gerrit vote-read failure preserves local dedup and holds the candidate in the next reconcile window.\n- [ ] Mutation proof: restoring the old local-dedup-first behavior makes the held-out restart regression fail.\n- [ ] Verification: focused review-bot tests pass.\n- [ ] Verification: `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] Verification: `make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] Verification: `make test` passes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786337550154846001,"uuid":"1f5a5067-fdc7-4038-8317-960790dab1c4"}